    "recommendations": "Ensuring the single access point and extended driveway remain clear of obstructions at all times could significantly improve response times and support effective apparatus positioning near the main building. Marking or enhancing the driveway entrance with clearly visible address signage would assist responders in locating the property quickly, particularly under low-visibility conditions. Where dense vegetation borders the driveway or circulation routes, maintaining adequate vertical and lateral clearance could support unimpeded apparatus movement. The unpaved circulation route could benefit from periodic attention to surface stability to support emergency vehicle movement. Given limited rear access, identifying and communicating an alternate pedestrian or personnel approach route to emergency services in advance may assist responder navigation during operations."
