    "recommendations": "Reducing brush and dense ground vegetation immediately surrounding the structure would improve defensible space and reduce fuel continuity in the area closest to the building. Where trees cluster near the structure, increasing separation between lower branches and ground-level vegetation could reduce vertical fuel continuity and may reduce structure exposure. Thinning or managing scattered shrubs and mixed vegetation within the immediate structure perimeter would further support defensible space goals. Along the long driveway, managing brush and ground vegetation on both sides could improve access route visibility and would support firefighter access and suppression operations during an incident. Maintaining a cleared, navigable driveway surface and ensuring adequate width and vertical clearance along its full length are priorities given the extended access route. Continued management of vegetation within the area surrounding the structure, particularly where brush is adjacent to the building, could meaningfully improve overall wildfire resilience and property preparedness."
